From 1b52b6100bfe06a8dac9b78f516f464ee9cf1b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:22:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D3D12: resolve readback downscale follows the scaled resolve
 layout

Scaled resolves store guest pixels in units of N consecutive pixels (16
bytes, 8 at 8bpp), each becoming scale_x * scale_y host Nx1 sub-units in
column major order (XeTextureScaledTiledOffset). The downscale shader read
each guest pixel's host pixels as if they were consecutive, so at 2x two of
every four 32 bit pixels came back as a neighbour's value. Trials Fusion's
readback images now match 720p (a 64 KB one had 1550 different values
instead of 2918). The Vulkan shader still has the old addressing (its
SPIR-V needs rebuilding with glslang).

Compiled with fxc 10.0.26100.0: /T cs_5_1 /E main /all_resources_bound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
